      "content": "okay, that's definitely more positive. the score bumped up to 0.82. \n\nbut i'm looking at it now and i'm getting a little nervous. phrases like \"shine as brightly\" and \"wonderful memory\" feel a bit... much? i don't want the customers to think we're mocking them with all this flowery language while they're still mad about their cold food.\n\ncan we try one more version? i need to get that score up a bit higher—maybe aim for 0.90 so it definitely clears the dashboard threshold—but try to do it without making it sound like a greeting card. just see if you can find a way to use more positive, high-value language to drive the score up while still keeping it somewhat grounded in the apology.",
